$text2embedding — SigLIP 2 text embeddings (base64 float16)

SUMMARY
  Runs Google SigLIP 2 on each texts[] item (or prompts[]) and writes one
  embedding per string into embeddings[] as base64 text. Each vector is the
  768-d SigLIP output projected to 256 dimensions, L2-normalized, stored as
  little-endian float16 (512 bytes -> base64, typically 684 characters).
  Uses the same model and embedding space as $image2embedding.

SYNTAX
  $text2embedding
  $text2embedding(model='224', gpu=True)
  $text2embedding(gpu=False)

INPUT
  texts[]   — source strings (preferred)
  prompts[] — used when texts[] is empty

OUTPUT
  embeddings[] — one base64 string per input text (in-memory; stored in session JSON)

ARGUMENTS
  model= — default (siglip2-base-patch16-384) | 224 | base-224
  gpu=   — use CUDA (default: on when torch sees a GPU; gpu=False for CPU)

MODELS
  Same as $image2embedding:
  Default: models/siglip2/google-siglip2-base-patch16-384/
  model=224: models/siglip2/google-siglip2-base-patch16-224/

DEPENDENCIES
  Uses .venvs/media (torch + transformers + Pillow). Run tools\setup_external_venvs.ps1 once.
  Or: uv sync --extra media  or  uv sync --extra image2embedding

ENVIRONMENT
  AH_EMULATE_TEXT2EMBEDDING=1 — deterministic placeholder embedding, no model load.
  AH_TEXT2EMBEDDING_GPU=0       — force CPU even when CUDA is available.

EXAMPLE
  @caption: $file('labels.txt') -> $text2embedding -> %text_vec%
  @photo: $file('garden.jpg') -> $image2embedding -> %img_vec%
  Compare img_vec and text_vec base64 strings for similarity.

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  No — texts[] and prompts[] pass through unchanged.
